<p>In the following discussions, we primarily focus on binary trees.</p>
<h2 id=3D"tree-traversals">Tree Traversals</h2>
<p><strong>Depth-first search (DFS)</strong><br>
DFS is a method for exploring all nodes of a tree by starting at the root a=
nd moving as far down a branch as possible, before backtracking to explore =
other branches.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a diagram illustrating Depth-First Search (=
DFS) traversal of a binary tree.  The tree consists of a root node labeled =
